  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1252 PM MST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\n19z surface analysis had low over central ND with water vapour \nloop suggesting upper low is starting to form over ND as shortwave\nwraps up. Shortwave is moisture starved, although some snow \naccumulations has occurred on the back side over northeastern \nWY/higher Black Hills. Strongest winds are across far southwestern\nSD early this afternoon.\n\nTonight, upper low pulls away with subsidence and drying in it's \nwake. Winds should die on schedule over southwestern SD. Over \nnorthwestern SD, main lower tropospheric wind max is just starting \nto emerge and thus, peak winds have not yet been met. Will continue \nheadlines as is based on latest probabilistic/observational trends. \nLows tonight will be near guidance.\n\nThursday/Friday, seasonally cool temperatures expected. Next cold\nfront arrives Friday with gusty northwest winds and colder \ntemperatures for the weekend. There is some hint stratus/fog could\ndevelop east of the Black Hills early Friday morning per \nsouth/southeast flow ahead of cold front. Upper trough slips \nthrough with cyclonic flow aloft suggesting PoPs warranted but \nmoisture will be limited. 5-10F below normal temperatures will \npersist into next week.",
